{
  "version": "4.9.0-beta.3",
  "changelog": {
    "Bug Fixes": [
      "Multi-account rolling keeps the current local roll boundary when a peer status response reports the next hour slightly early, preventing replenished rolls from being skipped.",
      "Snipe-only accounts keep their own pending claim reset until it is verified, preventing another preset's next cycle from causing an unnecessary $rt.",
      "Smart Timing waits through the exact claim reset boundary and keeps deferred claim candidates until a claim succeeds.",
      "Deferred roll processing ignores stale Kakera-only cards so claim handling cannot be delayed by expired buttons.",
      "Panic Claim now preserves the normal value floor for $rt, so low-value manual rolls cannot consume a restore unless they are an allowed wishlist target.",
      "Interrupted humanized reset waits now keep their original deadline unless a real status refresh or scheduled roll is pending, preventing repeated cached waits."
    ]
  },
